# A PLAYED RAID, FOUGHT LIVE (SETTLE.md S7). A yard that answered its warning, a
# palisade ring with a gate in it and three guns inside, is read, warned and
# probed. The party comes to the wall, the guns see over their own stakes and
# take the machine the wall holds, and the step is held without the player
# lifting a hand.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/raids_live.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --held=axe_felling --fail-downed --walled \
#     --holding=hut,plot,store,turret,turret,turret,battery_stack,battery_stack,solar_array \
#     --attention=0.5
#
# --holding stands the yard built with its cells full, --walled rings it in
# palisade with the gate the way the player faces, and --attention stages it at
# the probe line. Nothing is sent for a place nothing has read, so the clerk in
# frame 01 still has to read it.
zoom 12
coast calm
wait 0.8
spawn clerk
await noticed 14
await warned 25
wait 0.6
shot 01-the-warning with holding, piece:gate, piece:turret
# The window runs out, and they come out of the land for the yard.
hour 12.2
wait 1.6
await raid 40
await party 40
# The wall holds them at the ring (outside PARTY_AT_GATE, so no party_close):
# the frame is the moment a gun over the stakes first hits one of them there.
await turret_hit 90
wait 0.1
shot 02-the-party-at-the-wall-and-the-guns-fire with mob, piece:turret, piece:gate
await raider_down 60
# The working party down, the scout carries its report home and the step ends
# with the fight: held, with nothing struck.
await raid_ended:held 30
wait 0.6
shot 03-held with holding, piece:turret
